   "fontSize": 12.5,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "text": "per datagram   only datagrams whose source is the HOST, copied before\n               anything is parsed, so a copy is exact\n\none hand-built Ethernet + IPv4 + UDP frame per client, injected with\npcap_sendpacket; both checksums are computed, the UDP one over the IP\npseudo-header, so a copy is a complete valid datagram\n  Ethernet dst = the client's MAC   src = THIS adapter's own MAC\n               (spoofing that as well would teach every switch on the\n                way that the HOST lives on this port)\n  IP   src = the HOST, dst = the client\n  UDP  src = the HOST's port, dst = the client's port\nunicast: one frame per client, never broadcast\n\nclient MACs are resolved with SendARP on a background thread and\nre-resolved every few seconds, so a client switched on or replaced later\nis picked up on its own; one that stops answering drops out and the\nwindow counts how many are reachable\ndatagrams over 1472 B of payload are dropped and counted: a client's\ncapture filter matches one datagram, not a fragment chain\nthe adapter is found automatically - the one that owns the IG address,\nelse whichever the route to the HOST leaves by - and the window names it\nrelay counts: forwarded = reached at least one client, dropped = reached\nnone; clients that have not answered yet are neither",
   "originalText": "per datagram   only datagrams whose source is the HOST, copied before\n               anything is parsed, so a copy is exact\n\none hand-built Ethernet + IPv4 + UDP frame per client, injected with\npcap_sendpacket; both checksums are computed, the UDP one over the IP\npseudo-header, so a copy is a complete valid datagram\n  Ethernet dst = the client's MAC   src = THIS adapter's own MAC\n               (spoofing that as well would teach every switch on the\n                way that the HOST lives on this port)\n  IP   src = the HOST, dst = the client\n  UDP  src = the HOST's port, dst = the client's port\nunicast: one frame per client, never broadcast\n\nclient MACs are resolved with SendARP on a background thread and\nre-resolved every few seconds, so a client switched on or replaced later\nis picked up on its own; one that stops answering drops out and the\nwindow counts how many are reachable\ndatagrams over 1472 B of payload are dropped and counted: a client's\ncapture filter matches one datagram, not a fragment chain\nthe adapter is found automatically - the one that owns the IG address,\nelse whichever the route to the HOST leaves by - and the window names it\nrelay counts: forwarded = reached at least one client, dropped = reached\nnone; clients that have not answered yet are neither",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 12.5
  },
  {
   "id": "4188GsZQ19NGw1wWyHoa",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2360.0,
   "y": 2280.0,
   "width": 892.71,
   "height": 32.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "index": null,
   "seed": 904688670,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1128893284,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "created": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "Needs Npcap (wpcap.dll), loaded at run time rather than linked, so a PC without it still builds and runs as a plain IG; nothing here needs elevation.\nThe SOF link to the HOST is unaffected when the adapter cannot be opened.",
   "originalText": "Needs Npcap (wpcap.dll), loaded at run time rather than linked, so a PC without it still builds and runs as a plain IG; nothing here needs elevation.\nThe SOF link to the HOST is unaffected when the adapter cannot be opened.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 13
  },
  {
