   "fontSize": 19,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "9 - SOF rate and flow control",
   "originalText": "9 - SOF rate and flow control",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 19
  },
  {
   "id": "OH4OgAput5ag4eWvQjDO",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 120.0,
   "y": 2560.0,
   "width": 921.51,
   "height": 33.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "index": null,
   "seed": 888785717,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 213769042,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "created": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 13.5,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "The HOST owns the frame rate: one datagram per SOF, and its own frame counter advances about 53 times a second while the reference Master's\nSOF ran at ~100 Hz (an 8/12 ms alternation) - the Master asked for roughly twice the replies the HOST had frames to give.",
   "originalText": "The HOST owns the frame rate: one datagram per SOF, and its own frame counter advances about 53 times a second while the reference Master's\nSOF ran at ~100 Hz (an 8/12 ms alternation) - the Master asked for roughly twice the replies the HOST had frames to give.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 13.5
  },
  {
   "id": "Pg00m3ZJ3FvMlhfwpjCD",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 120.0,
   "y": 2610.0,
   "width": 620.0,
   "height": 265.625,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "index": null,
   "seed": 2041188743,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1835706938,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "created": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 12.5,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "text": "SOF rate default 150 Hz: every answer carries a fresh attitude (the position\ncomes on every other one), so how often the IG asks is how smoothly the\naircraft moves.\n\nFLOW CONTROL (default on, src\\SofPacer.h): a SOF is held back while the previous\none is still unanswered, so the stream fits whatever the HOST on site can\nabsorb, whatever number is typed in the rate box. A held-back frame is\ndropped, never replayed, so no mode of operation can turn the stream into a\nburst.\n  - a HOST that has never answered (startup, not yet woken) is transmitted\n    to at the full rate\n  - a SOF unanswered for 100 ms is followed by another anyway, so a HOST that\n    has dropped out still receives something to wake up on\n  - the limit is wall-clock, not a count of frames: a HOST answering less than\n    once per 100 ms sees at most ~10 requests a second whether the box says\n    150 or 6000. Counting frames would scale the retries with the rate -\n    exactly the runaway this exists to prevent",
   "originalText": "SOF rate default 150 Hz: every answer carries a fresh attitude (the position\ncomes on every other one), so how often the IG asks is how smoothly the\naircraft moves.\n\nFLOW CONTROL (default on, src\\SofPacer.h): a SOF is held back while the previous\none is still unanswered, so the stream fits whatever the HOST on site can\nabsorb, whatever number is typed in the rate box. A held-back frame is\ndropped, never replayed, so no mode of operation can turn the stream into a\nburst.\n  - a HOST that has never answered (startup, not yet woken) is transmitted\n    to at the full rate\n  - a SOF unanswered for 100 ms is followed by another anyway, so a HOST that\n    has dropped out still receives something to wake up on\n  - the limit is wall-clock, not a count of frames: a HOST answering less than\n    once per 100 ms sees at most ~10 requests a second whether the box says\n    150 or 6000. Counting frames would scale the retries with the rate -\n    exactly the runaway this exists to prevent",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 12.5
  },
  {
   "id": "6g6JYBW8ifbRDB4eCFdC",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 120.0,
   "y": 2905.0,
   "width": 937.44,
   "height": 50.625,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "index": null,
   "seed": 1021288085,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 754941999,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "created": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 13.5,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "The SOF's only live field is the HOST's frame counter echoed at offset 8. An IG-side count would drift from the HOST by (rate - 53) frames a second,\nwhich is what broke it above ~60 Hz. The window's Stream line names the mode - paced to the HOST or free-running - and adds \"which is the limit\"\nwhen it is the HOST setting the pace; --no-flow-control transmits on the rate alone, as the reference Master did.",
   "originalText": "The SOF's only live field is the HOST's frame counter echoed at offset 8. An IG-side count would drift from the HOST by (rate - 53) frames a second,\nwhich is what broke it above ~60 Hz. The window's Stream line names the mode - paced to the HOST or free-running - and adds \"which is the limit\"\nwhen it is the HOST setting the pace; --no-flow-control transmits on the rate alone, as the reference Master did.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 13.5
  },
  {
