   "fontSize": 19,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "10 - Terrain database (SRTM fallback)",
   "originalText": "10 - Terrain database (SRTM fallback)",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 19
  },
  {
   "id": "quB2N3LtoV0MHlHAqcJN",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1240.0,
   "y": 2560.0,
   "width": 565.75,
   "height": 171.875,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "index": null,
   "seed": 540616090,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1132454453,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "created": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 12.5,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "text": "terrain\\ beside the executable, or --terrain-dir.  Raw SRTM .hgt, one\n1 x 1 degree cell per file, named by the corner it starts at:\n  S07E106.hgt   covers 7..6 S, 106..107 E   (Jakarta)\n  S08E112.hgt   covers 8..7 S, 112..113 E   (Surabaya)\nSRTMGL1 (1 arc-sec, ~30 m, 3601x3601) and SRTMGL3 (3 arc-sec, ~90 m,\n1201x1201) are both accepted; the sample count comes from the file size\nsamples are signed 16-bit big-endian metres; row 0 is the northern edge\nand column 0 the western edge; -32768 is a void (interpolated around, or\nreported invalid when a point has nothing but voids)\nbilinear between the four surrounding samples; a tile is read in on first\nuse and kept - the window's TerrainDB line shows indexed / in memory / MB",
   "originalText": "terrain\\ beside the executable, or --terrain-dir.  Raw SRTM .hgt, one\n1 x 1 degree cell per file, named by the corner it starts at:\n  S07E106.hgt   covers 7..6 S, 106..107 E   (Jakarta)\n  S08E112.hgt   covers 8..7 S, 112..113 E   (Surabaya)\nSRTMGL1 (1 arc-sec, ~30 m, 3601x3601) and SRTMGL3 (3 arc-sec, ~90 m,\n1201x1201) are both accepted; the sample count comes from the file size\nsamples are signed 16-bit big-endian metres; row 0 is the northern edge\nand column 0 the western edge; -32768 is a void (interpolated around, or\nreported invalid when a point has nothing but voids)\nbilinear between the four surrounding samples; a tile is read in on first\nuse and kept - the window's TerrainDB line shows indexed / in memory / MB",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 12.5
  },
  {
   "id": "DsAV23qnT7XULCkw0Ht8",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1240.0,
   "y": 2775.0,
   "width": 920.5300000000001,
   "height": 65.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "index": null,
   "seed": 570111167,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 668494448,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "created": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "Two ways to get them.  tools\\get_terrain.ps1 downloads from the public AWS skadi mirror (-Points \"-6.13,106.66\" or -Tiles S07E106,S08E112), about 25\nMB per 1 arc-sec tile, so fetch only the box the aircraft flies in: the generic world model, quick, but SRTM predates the scenery.  tools\\TerrainBaker\noverlays the simulator's own ground heights on that base - plan -> probe -> survey -> compose -> terrain-sim\\*.hgt - sim-exact at the fields, runway\nflattening and all (probe/survey need Prepar3D with the add-on loaded; plan and compose need neither).",
   "originalText": "Two ways to get them.  tools\\get_terrain.ps1 downloads from the public AWS skadi mirror (-Points \"-6.13,106.66\" or -Tiles S07E106,S08E112), about 25\nMB per 1 arc-sec tile, so fetch only the box the aircraft flies in: the generic world model, quick, but SRTM predates the scenery.  tools\\TerrainBaker\noverlays the simulator's own ground heights on that base - plan -> probe -> survey -> compose -> terrain-sim\\*.hgt - sim-exact at the fields, runway\nflattening and all (probe/survey need Prepar3D with the add-on loaded; plan and compose need neither).",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 13
  },
  {
   "id": "h3Mpa6mMMvSuU69OhQvz",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1240.0,
   "y": 2890.0,
   "width": 910.2600000000001,
   "height": 32.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "index": null,
   "seed": 1389322632,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 911189041,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "created": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "Calibration: SRTM heights are orthometric (EGM96) and the sim's datum is its own; the two matched to ~2 m at Juanda in testing. --terrain-offset <m>\nshifts every database height if a site shows a constant bias - the database only, never FSUIPC and never a sim height.",
   "originalText": "Calibration: SRTM heights are orthometric (EGM96) and the sim's datum is its own; the two matched to ~2 m at Juanda in testing. --terrain-offset <m>\nshifts every database height if a site shows a constant bias - the database only, never FSUIPC and never a sim height.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseFontSize": 13
  },
  {
